  "description": "Proposed erection of a mixed use building varying in height from 1 and 3 storeys adjacent to the river and 5 storeys adjacent to the Waggon & Horses Public House - stepping up through 4, 5, 6 and 7 storeys - and rising to a height of 8 storeys along Kew Bridge Road and Kew Bridge . On the junction of these two roads  the 8 storeys height would rise with an additional set-back 2 storey penthouse storey on top (a total of 10 floors). The development comprises parking and refuse and recycling facilities at basement level, commercial uses (B1, A1, A3 & D1 and a Spa) at ground floor level and 238 residential flats on floors 1-9 - 97 (40%) of which are affordable.\r\n\r\n"
